{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California application screening fee cap","requirement":"A landlord may charge an application screening fee not exceeding actual out-of-pocket costs and no more than $30 per applicant; must provide an itemized receipt, refund unused amounts, and give a copy of the credit report within 7 days.","key_value":"$30 per applicant, CPI adjustable","coverage_conditions":"Applies to any landlord of residential rental property and to applicants, including guarantors or cosigners, for residential housing units.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"An application screening fee is charged to an applicant; no fee may be charged when the landlord knows or should know no rental unit is available or will be available within a reasonable period.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"In no case shall the amount of the application screening fee charged by the landlord or their agent be greater than thirty dollars ($30) per applicant. The thirty dollar ($30) application screening fee may be adjusted annually by the landlord or their agent commensurate with an increase in the Consumer Price Index, beginning on January 1, 1998.","interaction":"Operates notwithstanding Section 1950.5; does not preempt federal or state housing assistance program deposit and fee rules.","relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California application screening order and criteria","requirement":"A landlord or agent who charges an application screening fee must consider completed applications in the order received, give screening criteria in writing, approve the first applicant meeting them, and not charge a fee until the application is actually considered.","key_value":"First qualified applicant approved; fee only when considered","coverage_conditions":"Applies to any landlord of residential rental property and to applicants, including guarantors or cosigners, for residential housing units.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Screening process applies when an application screening fee is collected; refund within 7 days if application not considered; return fee within 7 days of selecting tenant or 30 days of application, whichever first.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"(i) Completed applications are considered, as provided for in the landlord’s established screening criteria, in the order in which the completed applications were received. The landlord’s screening criteria shall be provided to the applicant in writing together with the application form.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
